DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(cos(x))^2+2*(x^3)+2");
$fun_1 = Formula("(x^2+2*x+2)-3");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("[1, 6] - ((-infinity, infinity) - {7, 10}) U {1, 6}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{7, 10} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {7, 10}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 6])");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("{1, 6} U {1, 6} U ([1, 6]) U ({1, 6} U {7, 10})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("((-infinity, 18] U (-infinity, 18]) U ((-infinity, 18]) U {-8, 0, 1, 2, 6}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-8, 0, 1, 2, 6} U {-8, 0, 1, 2, 6}");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("(-infinity, 18] U (-infinity, 17)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`10+2-8-12`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(-8.),width=>4}
---

[`19+16-1+18*5`] is equal to [_____]{Real(124.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-8, 0, 1, 2, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 18\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x < 17\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B \cup B) \cup (B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{7, 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 6\}`]
- [`C = \{1, 6\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap A \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cap A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`C \cup C \cup (B) \cup (C \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, 7, -1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -9, 7, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -5, -3, -1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-5, -3, -1>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, -3, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, 7, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, -3, -1>") x Compute("<-9, 7, 2>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, 7, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-9, 7, 2>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, 4, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 3, -8, -3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, 4, -8>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, 4, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, -8, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, -8, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<3, -8, -3>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>5)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
